message: If you use this work, please cite it as below.
title: "Algebraic ratios between exact prime-race crossings"
abstract: "Across the two hosts at most three exact hits of magnitude 1.9735 share algebraic starting-height ratios. At least 1,830 pairs through one million have transcendental quotient. On 547/727 at least 3,274 inequivalent hits finish below exp(12500). The general high-range bound and the geometric-sampling rank apply to both fields."
